            <ArticleTitle>Nasal polyps.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>264-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nasal polyps are as common as adult onset asthma and unilateral polyps require histological examination. Medical therapy with corticosteroids should be tried before surgery. The anatomy should be demonstrated with computed tomography before endoscopic surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
